er/id #uuid "ca603544-ca62-53c2-af73-bc3d74434242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517071}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517036} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea84f414-c5fa-53e3-8ecf-7bb0e3512d21" :answer-field/key "The point $(\\frac{-11\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "90b0a035-4445-5d93-8397-5dbf069c4ed0" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{-11\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement “The point $(\\frac{-11\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph” is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement “$x=15\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote” is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{-13\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement “$x=\\frac{-13\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf80cc-ab53-5783-bcc2-db059f3f00b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517030} {:answer/id #uuid "b139766e-16ba-5da1-81f4-45b69bcf78f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517063} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db197b0-d4aa-53f5-a73a-5cd1a621edb1" :answer-field/key "$x=-11\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/