⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521718}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521688} :answer-field/id #uuid "854ed5c8-bf23-5931-b481-8a38951b43b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4f9f3451-ede1-5210-8b07-6d5429ad7a60" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(4 x - 5 y^{2})\\,i+(- 10 x y + 12 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}) & =(4 \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) - 5 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{2})\\,i+(- 10 \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) + 12 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right))\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{85}{9}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\frac{13}{3}\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{9},- \\frac{13}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot ⟨x-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right),\\,y-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{85}{9},- \\frac{13}{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨x - \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{3}⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "5706501c-de86-5634-87a7-ddcfe0773c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218