e line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n-\\oint_C(P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y)=\\oint_Cy\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\nr'(t)=⟨17\\cos(t),\\,-17\\sin(t)⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\oint_Cy\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}17\\cos(t)\\cdot 17\\cos(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}289\\cos^{2}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b85814f-cef1-50ce-a0c2-e193caf5926b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522940} {:answer/id #uuid "4de1dc13-89bc-5d8f-ac26-038f1d188087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 24 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522951} {:answer/id #uuid "7763e82b-d4bc-51ac-a9b0-38a352a32d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522968} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b48ef2-128e-5882-aeb3-90e0fe45e532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522985} {:answer/id #uuid "bed32c84-b998-5ffc-b9fc-2d52cb2fca72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522990} :answer-field/id #uuid "cefab37e-fc9a-5602-b089-f4a73bceb50a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "122914c3-d4ec-5c1f-8cab-a9260c5fdc07" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efb35e6552df72236d914018d36b1e582611a91de649cbe69c182b0469e5c15d.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the